    "lru": "All host namespaces in one renderer share one weighted LRU. Lookup touches the entry. Entries are evicted for byte, process-entry or host-entry pressure; host IDs cannot multiply the byte limit.",
    "charge": "Checked/saturating accounting includes generated SKP data, Base64/resource/error strings, reserved font/range vector storage, nested string capacities, EncodedPicture/SkData/control and cache-index estimates. Conservative cache-owner charge, not measured allocator usage.",
    "pins": "Returned pointers alias a charged allocation control block. Eviction and host retirement detach cache ownership, but the reservation remains until the final returned alias releases and its payload destructor finishes. Snapshot/layer owners pin the allocation through native payload delivery.",
    "fallback": "Encoding and retired-payload destruction run outside the registry mutex. Oversized, stale-owner, untracked shared input or fully pinned budget returns the current complete encoding uncached; it cannot become a false cache/hash-only hit. Victim retries are finite and do not wait for readers.",
    "telemetry": "captureHosts reports cache, admitted resident, retired/cached pin bytes, peak, limits, admissions, evictions and each bypass reason. Scope is explicitly renderer-process; host index estimate is separately reported."
